{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef _clean_string(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes all space characters from the input string.\"\"\"\n    return s.replace(' ', '')\n\n\ndef _find_top_level_groups(cleaned_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Identifies and extracts top-level, balanced parenthesis groups using a balance counter.\"\"\"\n    groups: List[str] = []\n    balance: int = 0\n    current_group_chars: List[str] = []\n\n    for char in cleaned_string:\n        if char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n\n        current_group_chars.append(char)\n\n        if balance == 0 and current_group_chars:\n            groups.append(\"\".join(current_group_chars))\n            current_group_chars = []\n\n    return groups\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Separates distinct, top-level groups of nested parentheses from an input string into a list of strings.\n    It ignores spaces and ensures each separated group is balanced.\n    \"\"\"\n    cleaned_string = _clean_string(paren_string)\n    list_of_groups = _find_top_level_groups(cleaned_string)\n    return list_of_groups\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string containing multiple groups of nested parentheses. Your goal is to\n    separate those group into separate strings and return the list of those.\n    Separate groups are balanced (each open brace is properly closed) and not nested within each other\n    Ignore any spaces in the input string.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_groups = []\n    current_group = \"\"\n    balance = 0\n\n    for char in paren_string:\n        if char == ' ':\n            continue\n        elif char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n            current_group += char\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n            current_group += char\n            if balance == 0:\n                result_groups.append(current_group)\n                current_group = \"\"\n    return result_groups\n```"}
