{"task_id": "HumanEval/21", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef rescale_to_unit(numbers: List[float]) -> List[float]:\n    \"\"\" Given list of numbers (of at least two elements), apply a linear transform\n    such that the smallest number becomes 0.0 and the largest becomes 1.0.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_val = min(numbers)\n    max_val = max(numbers)\n\n    if min_val == max_val:\n        # If all numbers are identical, map all to 0.0 as per design.\n        return [0.0] * len(numbers)\n    else:\n        scale_factor = max_val - min_val\n        # Apply the linear transformation formula for each number.\n        return [(x - min_val) / scale_factor for x in numbers]\n```"}
