{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Return a list of prime factors for the input integer `n`, ordered from smallest to largest.\n    Each factor is listed according to its multiplicity.\n    >>> factorize(8)\n    [2, 2, 2]\n    >>> factorize(25)\n    [5, 5]\n    >>> factorize(70)\n    [2, 5, 7]\n    \"\"\"\n    factors = []\n    temp_n = n\n\n    # Handle factor 2\n    while temp_n % 2 == 0:\n        factors.append(2)\n        temp_n //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors starting from 3\n    d = 3\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            temp_n //= d\n        d += 2  # Increment by 2 to check only odd numbers\n\n    # If temp_n is still greater than 1, it must be the largest prime factor\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n\n    return factors\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef _map_symbol_to_beats(symbol: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Maps a musical note symbol to its corresponding beat duration.\"\"\"\n    if symbol == 'o':\n        return 4  # Whole note\n    elif symbol == 'o|':\n        return 2  # Half note\n    elif symbol == '.|':\n        return 1  # Quarter note\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown musical note symbol: {symbol}\")\n\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string representing musical notes in a special ASCII format.\n    Your task is to parse this string and return list of integers corresponding to how many beats does each\n    not last.\n\n    Here is a legend:\n    'o' - whole note, lasts four beats\n    'o|' - half note, lasts two beats\n    '.|' - quater note, lasts one beat\n\n    >>> parse_music('o o| .| o| o| .| .| .| .| o o')\n    [4, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 4, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    # Split the input string by spaces to get individual note symbols.\n    note_symbols = music_string.split(' ')\n\n    # Map each symbol to its beat duration.\n    beat_durations: List[int] = []\n    for symbol in note_symbols:\n        if symbol: # Handle potential empty strings from multiple spaces.\n            beat_durations.append(_map_symbol_to_beats(symbol))\n\n    return beat_durations\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/26", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef remove_duplicates(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" From a list of integers, remove all elements that occur more than once.\n    Keep order of elements left the same as in the input.\n    >>> remove_duplicates([1, 2, 3, 2, 4])\n    [1, 3, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for num in numbers:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    result = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            result.append(num)\n    return result\n```"}
