{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a new list l_prime, initially a copy of l.\n    l_prime = list(l)\n\n    # Collect values and their original indices from positions divisible by three.\n    collected_values = []\n    divisible_indices = []\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            collected_values.append(l[i])\n            divisible_indices.append(i)\n\n    # Sort the collected values in ascending order.\n    collected_values.sort()\n\n    # Place the sorted values back into l_prime at their original divisible-by-three indices.\n    sorted_value_cursor = 0\n    for index_to_update in divisible_indices:\n        l_prime[index_to_update] = collected_values[sorted_value_cursor]\n        sorted_value_cursor += 1\n\n    return l_prime\n```"}
