{"task_id": "HumanEval/36", "solution": "```python\ndef fizz_buzz(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the total occurrences of the digit '7' in positive integers strictly less than n,\n    which are divisible by either 11 or 13.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_divisible_by_11_or_13(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is divisible by 11 or 13.\"\"\"\n        return num % 11 == 0 or num % 13 == 0\n\n    def _count_digit_7(num: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the occurrences of the digit '7' in a number's decimal representation.\"\"\"\n        return str(num).count('7')\n\n    total_7s_count = 0\n    for x in range(1, n):\n        if _is_divisible_by_11_or_13(x):\n            total_7s_count += _count_digit_7(x)\n\n    return total_7s_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_even(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function sorts elements at even indices in a list while preserving odd-indexed elements.\"\"\"\n    output_list = list(l)\n\n    even_values = []\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            even_values.append(l[i])\n\n    even_values.sort()\n\n    sorted_even_idx = 0\n    for i in range(len(output_list)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            output_list[i] = even_values[sorted_even_idx]\n            sorted_even_idx += 1\n\n    return output_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_even(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the odd indicies, while its values at the even indicies are equal\n    to the values of the even indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = l.copy()\n    even_indexed_values = []\n\n    # Extract all values from even indices\n    for i in range(0, len(l), 2):\n        even_indexed_values.append(l[i])\n\n    # Sort the extracted even-indexed values\n    even_indexed_values.sort()\n\n    # Place the sorted values back into the even indices of the result list\n    sorted_idx = 0\n    for i in range(0, len(result_list), 2):\n        result_list[i] = even_indexed_values[sorted_idx]\n        sorted_idx += 1\n\n    return result_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "```python\ndef _decode_block(block: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Helper function to decode a single block.\n    It cyclically shifts 3-character blocks to the right.\"\"\"\n    if len(block) == 3:\n        # To reverse 'bca' back to 'abc', take block[2] + block[0] + block[1]\n        return block[2] + block[0] + block[1]\n    return block\n\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Decodes a string by reversing cyclic shifts on 3-character blocks.\n    It processes the input string in fixed-size blocks.\"\"\"\n    decoded_parts = []\n    for i in range(0, len(s), 3):\n        block = s[i:i+3]\n        decoded_parts.append(_decode_block(block))\n    return ''.join(decoded_parts)\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_cyclic function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Split string to groups. Each of length 3.\n    # Reusing the splitting logic from encode_cyclic\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n\n    decoded_groups = []\n    for group in groups:\n        # Reverse cycle elements in each group if it has 3 elements.\n        # This is achieved by moving the last character to the front.\n        if len(group) == 3:\n            decoded_groups.append(group[-1] + group[:-1])\n        else:\n            # If group has fewer elements than 3, it remains unchanged as per encode_cyclic.\n            decoded_groups.append(group)\n\n    return \"\".join(decoded_groups)\n```"}
