{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_perfect_square(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is a perfect square.\"\"\"\n    if num < 0:\n        return False\n    if num == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # Manually calculate integer square root and check.\n    x = 0\n    while x * x <= num:\n        if x * x == num:\n            return True\n        x += 1\n    return False\n\ndef _is_fibonacci(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a given number is a Fibonacci number.\"\"\"\n    # A positive integer x is Fibonacci if 5x^2 + 4 or 5x^2 - 4 is a perfect square.\n    return _is_perfect_square(5 * num * num + 4) or _is_perfect_square(5 * num * num - 4)\n\ndef _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is a prime number.\"\"\"\n    if num < 2:\n        return False\n    if num == 2 or num == 3:\n        return True\n    if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Check for factors from 5 onwards using an optimized loop.\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= num:\n        if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\\\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True\n\ndef prime_fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    num = 1 # Start checking from 1, as numbers below 2 are not prime.\n\n    while True:\n        num += 1 # Increment to check the next natural number\n        if _is_fibonacci(num):\n            if _is_prime(num):\n                count += 1\n                if count == n:\n                    return num\n```"}
