{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence using an iterative dynamic programming approach.\n    It handles base cases for n=0, 1, 2, 3 and applies the recurrence relation for n > 3.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    dp_array = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp_array[0] = 0\n    dp_array[1] = 0\n    dp_array[2] = 2\n    dp_array[3] = 0\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        dp_array[i] = dp_array[i-1] + dp_array[i-2] + dp_array[i-3] + dp_array[i-4]\n\n    return dp_array[n]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    The list is assumed to be non-empty and contain only numeric values.\n    \"\"\"\n    l_sorted = sorted(l)\n    n = len(l_sorted)\n\n    if n % 2 != 0:\n        # Odd number of elements: median is the middle element.\n        return float(l_sorted[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # Even number of elements: median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = l_sorted[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = l_sorted[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0"}
