{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\ndef modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p (be aware of numerics).\n    This function uses modular exponentiation by squaring for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p  # Initialize base as 2, reduced by modulus p.\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:  # If n is odd, multiply result by current base.\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p  # Square the base.\n        n //= 2  # Halve the exponent n.\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\ndef modp(n: int, p: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p efficiently using exponentiation by squaring.\n    This function applies modular arithmetic at each step to prevent numerical overflow.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 % p\n\n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        n //= 2\n\n    return result\n```"}
