{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list) -> float | int:\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n\n    Args:\n        l (list): A list of numerical values (int or float).\n\n    Returns:\n        float | int: The calculated median.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input list is empty.\n        TypeError: If the list contains non-numerical elements.\n\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    8.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    for item in l:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be numerical values (int or float).\")\n\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\ndef monotonic(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n    Handles empty and single-element lists as True.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_increasing = True\n    is_decreasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if l[i] < l[i-1]:\n            is_increasing = False\n        if l[i] > l[i-1]:\n            is_decreasing = False\n\n        # Optimization: if both flags are false, it's neither\n        if not is_increasing and not is_decreasing:\n            return False\n\n    return is_increasing or is_decreasing\n```"}
