{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "```python\ndef vowels_count(s):\n    \"\"\"Write a function vowels_count which takes a string representing\n    a word as input and returns the number of vowels in the string.\n    Vowels in this case are 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'. Here, 'y' is also a\n    vowel, but only when it is at the end of the given word.\n\n    Example:\n    >>> vowels_count(\"abcde\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"ACEDY\")\n    3\n    >>> vowels_count(\"\")\n    0\n    >>> vowels_count(\"rhythm\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"fly\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"type\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"aeiouAEIOU\")\n    10\n    >>> vowels_count(\"hEllO wOrLd\")\n    3\n    >>> vowels_count(\"python\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"mystery\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"a\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"z\")\n    0\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n    n = len(s_lower)\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(s_lower):\n        if char in 'aeiou':\n            count += 1\n        elif char == 'y' and i == n - 1:\n            count += 1\n\n    return count\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "```python\ndef vowels_count(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Write a function vowels_count which takes a string representing\n    a word as input and returns the number of vowels in the string.\n    Vowels in this case are 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'. Here, 'y' is also a\n    vowel, but only when it is at the end of the given word.\n\n    The counting is case-insensitive.\n\n    Example:\n    >>> vowels_count(\"abcde\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"ACEDY\")\n    3\n    >>> vowels_count(\"hello\") # Standard vowels\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"rhythm\") # 'y' at end\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"sky\") # 'y' at end\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"type\") # 'y' not at end\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"gym\") # 'y' not at end, no other vowels\n    0\n    >>> vowels_count(\"aeiou\") # All standard vowels\n    5\n    >>> vowels_count(\"AEIOU\") # All standard vowels, uppercase\n    5\n    >>> vowels_count(\"rhythms\") # 'y' not at end, no other vowels\n    0\n    >>> vowels_count(\"\") # Empty string\n    0\n    >>> vowels_count(\"bcdfgh\") # No vowels\n    0\n    >>> vowels_count(\"syzygy\") # Multiple 'y's, only last counts\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"mystery\") # Multiple 'y's, only last counts\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"AeiOuY\") # Mixed case, 'y' at end\n    6\n    \"\"\"\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n    count = 0\n    vowels = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(s_lower):\n        if char in vowels:\n            count += 1\n        elif char == 'y' and i == len(s_lower) - 1:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
