{"task_id": "HumanEval/67", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef fruit_distribution(s, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of mango fruits in a basket.\n    It parses the input string for apples and oranges, then subtracts their sum from the total.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Extracts the number of apples from the input string using regex.\n    apples = int(re.search(r'(\\d+)\\s+apples', s).group(1))\n\n    # Extracts the number of oranges from the input string using regex.\n    oranges = int(re.search(r'(\\d+)\\s+oranges', s).group(1))\n\n    # Calculates the number of mangoes.\n    mangoes = n - (apples + oranges)\n    return mangoes\n```"}
