{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "```python\ndef _split_into_sentences(text: str, delimiters: tuple) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Splits a given text into sentences based on specified delimiters.\n    The delimiters are included in the resulting sentence fragments.\n    \"\"\"\n    sentences = []\n    current_sentence_start = 0\n    for i, char in enumerate(text):\n        if char in delimiters:\n            sentence = text[current_sentence_start : i + 1]\n            # Add sentence if it's not empty after stripping whitespace,\n            # which helps handle multiple adjacent delimiters.\n            if sentence.strip():\n                sentences.append(sentence)\n            current_sentence_start = i + 1\n\n    # Add any remaining part as a sentence if no delimiter at the very end\n    if current_sentence_start < len(text):\n        remaining_part = text[current_sentence_start:]\n        if remaining_part.strip():\n            sentences.append(remaining_part)\n\n    return sentences\n\ndef _starts_with_i(sentence_text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a sentence starts with the word 'I' (case-sensitive).\n    Checks for 'I' after trimming leading whitespace, followed by a non-alphabetic character or end of sentence.\n    \"\"\"\n    trimmed_sentence = sentence_text.lstrip()\n\n    if not trimmed_sentence:\n        return False\n\n    if trimmed_sentence[0] == 'I':\n        # If the sentence is just 'I' (e.g., \"I\", \"I.\", \"I?\").\n        if len(trimmed_sentence) == 1:\n            return True\n        # Check if 'I' is followed by a non-alphabetic character, enforcing word boundary.\n        elif not trimmed_sentence[1].isalpha():\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef is_bored(S: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    You'll be given a string of words, and your task is to count the number\n    of boredoms. A boredom is a sentence that starts with the word \"I\".\n    Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n\n    For example:\n    >>> is_bored(\"Hello world\")\n    0\n    >>> is_bored(\"The sky is blue. The sun is shining. I love this weather\")\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n    bored_count = 0\n    delimiters = ('.', '?', '!')\n\n    sentences = _split_into_sentences(S, delimiters)\n\n    for sentence in sentences:\n        if _starts_with_i(sentence):\n            bored_count += 1\n\n    return bored_count\n```"}
