{"task_id": "HumanEval/152", "solution": "```python\ndef compare(game: list[int], guess: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Compares actual game scores with user guesses and returns an array of absolute differences.\n    Returns 0 if the guess was correct, otherwise the absolute difference.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for i in range(len(game)):\n        if guess[i] == game[i]:\n            results.append(0)\n        else:\n            results.append(abs(guess[i] - game[i]))\n    return results\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "```python\ndef generate_integers(a: int, b: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a list of even single-digit numbers between a and b (inclusive),\n    in ascending order. Returns an empty list if no such numbers exist.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = min(a, b)\n    end = max(a, b)\n\n    result = []\n\n    # Iterate through the inclusive range [start, end].\n    for num in range(start, end + 1):\n        # Filter for even and single-digit numbers.\n        if num % 2 == 0 and 0 <= num <= 9:\n            result.append(num)\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/162", "solution": "```python\nimport hashlib\n\ndef string_to_md5(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string 'text', return its md5 hash equivalent string.\n    If 'text' is an empty string, return None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return None\n\n    md5_hash_object = hashlib.md5()\n    md5_hash_object.update(text.encode('utf-8'))\n    return md5_hash_object.hexdigest()\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "```python\nEVEN_SINGLE_DIGITS = [0, 2, 4, 6, 8]\n\ndef generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine the inclusive range from inputs a and b.\n    min_val, max_val = min(a, b), max(a, b)\n\n    # Filter the predefined even single-digits that fall within the determined range.\n    # The constant list is already sorted, so filtering preserves ascending order.\n    filtered_digits = [\n        digit for digit in EVEN_SINGLE_DIGITS\n        if min_val <= digit <= max_val\n    ]\n\n    return filtered_digits\n```\n"}
