{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n\n    >>> largest_divisor(15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    # Iterate downwards from n // 2 to 1 to find the largest proper divisor.\n    for i in range(n // 2, 0, -1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return i\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/159", "solution": "def eat(number, need, remaining):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates total carrots eaten and remaining stock after a rabbit's meal.\n    Considers initial eaten carrots, needed carrots, and available stock.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    consumed_carrots = min(need, remaining)\n    total_eaten_carrots = number + consumed_carrots\n    carrots_left_in_stock = remaining - consumed_carrots\n\n    return [total_eaten_carrots, carrots_left_in_stock]"}
